ISSUE: sveltejs/svelte#18924: Extra node before a nested <svelte:boundary> throws a TypeError during hydration instead of recovering

### Describe the bug

Follow-up to #18840 / #18841.

#18841 lets the hydration mismatch signal pass through boundaries so `hydrate()` can recover. There is one case it doesn't cover: when the unexpected node sits exactly where a nested boundary's opening comment should be.

The boundary reads `comment.data.startsWith(...)` on whatever node is at that position. If it's an element, `data` is undefined, so it throws

```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'startsWith')
```

That is a normal error, not the hydration signal, so a parent boundary with `failed` / `onerror` catches it. No warning, no recovery, the parent's fallback renders.

How I ran into it: SvelteKit 3 wraps every route node in a boundary, and a browser extension was adding an element to the page before hydration. The whole app got replaced by the error page with a 500. #18841 fixes that for most positions, but if the element lands as the first child of an element whose first child is a boundary (the start of `<main>` in a layout, for example), it still ends up on the error page.

Expected: handled like any other hydration mismatch (warn and recover).

The read is in `packages/svelte/src/internal/client/dom/blocks/boundary.js`:

```js
const comment = /** @type {Comment} */ (this.#hydrate_open);
// ...
const server_rendered_failed = comment.data.startsWith(HYDRATION_START_FAILED);
```

A check that the node is a comment before reading it (and going down the mismatch path if not) would probably be enough. Happy to send a PR if that sounds right.

