ISSUE: sveltejs/svelte#19044: Fallback roles in `role` trigger false a11y warnings

### Describe the bug

The `role` attribute can list fallback roles, for example `role="switch checkbox"`. Browsers and assistive technology use the first token that is a valid role. Svelte supports this since #8045: each token is checked for `a11y_unknown_role`.

The element-level checks that run after that still treat the whole attribute value as one role. A value like `"switch checkbox"` matches no known role, so the element is treated as if it had no interactive role. This produces warnings that don't apply:

- `a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex` on `<div role="switch checkbox" tabindex="0">`
- `a11y_no_static_element_interactions` ("must have an ARIA role") on a `<div>` that has a role
- `a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions` on `<div role="none presentation" onclick={...}>`

`a11y_role_supports_aria_props` is also skipped for these elements, so an unsupported ARIA attribute isn't reported.

The same happens when the value has leading or trailing whitespace, such as `role=" button "`.

### Reproduction

```svelte
<script>
	function handler() {}
</script>

<div role="switch checkbox" aria-checked="false" tabindex="0" onclick={handler} onkeydown={handler}></div>
<div role="none presentation" onclick={handler}></div>
```

The first element reports `a11y_no_noninteractive_tabindex` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`. With `role="switch"` it reports nothing. The second element reports `a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`. With `role="none"` it reports nothing.

### Logs

_No response_

### System Info

```shell
svelte 5.57.2 (main)
```

### Severity

annoyance

