ISSUE: axios/axios#11114: forEach() throws when interceptors.handlers is set to null

:surfer:

## Describe the issue

Regression from #11087 (merged, not yet released). `syncHandlerEntries()` reads `handlers.length` before checking that `handlers` exists, so setting the array to a falsy value makes every subsequent request throw instead of behaving as it did in 1.19.0.

`clear()` already guards with `if (this.handlers)`, which is why I took a falsy array to be a tolerated state.

To be clear this is not another attempt at #11070, which #11087 fixed. It is a crash introduced by that fix.

## Example code

```js
import axios from 'axios';

axios.interceptors.request.use(config => config);
axios.interceptors.request.handlers = null;

await axios.get('https://example.com');
```

## Expected behavior

The request goes out and the interceptor is skipped, as on v1.19.0. `utils.forEach` returns early on nullish input, so `forEach()` used to be a no-op here.

## Actual behavior

```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'length')
    at syncHandlerEntries (lib/core/InterceptorManager.js:31:39)
    at InterceptorManager.forEach (lib/core/InterceptorManager.js:135:5)
```

`undefined` behaves the same way. Because `_request` calls `forEach` on both managers, every request fails once `handlers` has been set to a falsy value.

Two smaller things from the same change, if they are worth folding into one PR:

* `eject(String(id))` now silently leaves the interceptor installed. The old array lookup coerced the string, a `Map` lookup does not.
* Once `trimHandlers` has run, ids are no longer array indices, so `handlers[id]` can be `undefined`. `use`, `eject`, `use` yields id `1` with its handler at index `0`. `tests/unit/core/InterceptorManager.test.js:32` indexes by id and passes only because nothing below those slots gets trimmed.

## Environment

- Axios version: `v1.x` at 529ce70 (after v1.19.0)
- Adapter: http (also reproduces with xhr and fetch, the throw is in `_request` before adapter selection)
- Runtime: Node 24.16.0
- OS: Windows 11
- Additional context: reproduced against the repo working copy, `npx vitest run --project unit` otherwise green at 986 tests

