ISSUE: webpack/webpack#23007: rule.extractSourceMap leaves //# sourceMappingURL comments in the bundle when devtool is disabled

### Have you used AI?

Yes

### Which part of webpack is affected?

sourcemaps

### Bug Description

With `module.rules[].extractSourceMap: true`, webpack strips the `//# sourceMappingURL=...` comment from a module and uses the referenced map, but only when source maps are enabled (`devtool` set). With `devtool: false` the module is passed through untouched and the comment ends up in the bundle.

`source-map-loader`, which `extractSourceMap` replaces, removes the comment regardless of `devtool`.


### Link to Minimal Reproduction and steps to reproduce

https://github.com/[Knagis/webpack-extractSourceMap](https://github.com/Knagis/webpack-extractSourceMap)

1. run `npm i`
2. run `npm run repro`

### Expected Behavior

`//# sourceMappingURL=` comments are removed always, even if devtool is disabled as the comment can trigger browser to download non-existent files.

### Actual Behavior

When devtool is disabled, the comment remains in output. When devtool is enabled, comment is removed.

### Environment

```shell
node: 26.9.0
webpack: 5.112.2
```

### Is this a regression?

No

### Last Working Version

_No response_

### Additional Context

_No response_

