ISSUE: mrdoob/three.js#35122: WebGPURenderer: Materials use the shader of the camera type that renders them first

### Description

Related: #34982, #35072

When one scene is rendered with a perspective and an orthographic camera, materials use the shader built for the camera type that renders them first breaking depth effects, specular lighting, logarithmic depth and point and sprite sizes.

**Cause**

These places check the type of `builder.camera` at build time:

- `ViewportDepthNode`: `depth` and `linearDepth( value )`, so `viewportLinearDepth`
- `positionViewDirection`, which the BRDFs use for specular lighting
- `NodeMaterial.setupDepth()` with `logarithmicDepthBuffer`
- `PointsNodeMaterial` with `sizeAttenuation: true`
- `SpriteNodeMaterial` with `sizeAttenuation: false`

The camera type is not part of the render object or node builder cache keys, so all cameras get the shader of the first one.

### Reproduction steps

1. Render a scene with a `PerspectiveCamera`.
2. Render the same scene with an `OrthographicCamera` and the same renderer, for example into a second `CanvasTarget`.
3. The orthographic view uses the shaders built for the perspective camera. Rendering the orthographic camera first breaks the perspective view instead.

### Code

```js
const scene = new THREE.Scene();

const perspectiveCamera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera( 50, 1, 0.1, 100 );
const orthographicCamera = new THREE.OrthographicCamera( - 2, 2, 2, - 2, 0.1, 100 );

// Also affected: lit materials (specular), viewportLinearDepth, logarithmicDepthBuffer
// and PointsNodeMaterial with sizeAttenuation: true.
const sprite = new THREE.Sprite( new THREE.SpriteNodeMaterial( { sizeAttenuation: false } ) );
sprite.position.z = - 10;
scene.add( sprite );

const renderer = new THREE.WebGPURenderer();
await renderer.init();

renderer.render( scene, perspectiveCamera ); // builds the sprite shader for a perspective camera
renderer.render( scene, orthographicCamera ); // reuses it, so the sprite is 10 times too large
```

### Live example

* [Depth effect: perspective and orthographic views of one scene](https://jsfiddle.net/rxs3qcdz/1/)
* [Points and sprites: perspective camera first, then orthographic](https://jsfiddle.net/58qy1tew/1/)

### Screenshots

**Depth effect** ([fiddle](https://jsfiddle.net/rxs3qcdz/1/))

Two `CanvasTarget`s render one scene: view 1 with a perspective camera, view 2 with an orthographic camera. The water shows foam where its depth is close to the depth behind it (`viewportLinearDepth`). On `dev`, view 2 converts its depth buffer as perspective depth and the water turns white.

| Current (`dev`) | Expected |
| --- | --- |
| <img width="776" height="396" alt="On dev, the water in the orthographic view is white" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65b7d436-7bfc-4621-8e4b-d3b66993c701" /> | <img width="776" height="396" alt="Foam only around the columns in both views" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03ac92ee-536b-470d-a1f9-4da4eb86d87d" /> |

**Points and sprites** ([fiddle](https://jsfiddle.net/58qy1tew/1/))

Each row renders one scene with a perspective camera first, then an orthographic camera. In an orthographic view, all points and all sprites should have the same size. On `dev`, the orthographic points (`PointsNodeMaterial`, `sizeAttenuation: true`) shrink with distance and the sprites (`SpriteNodeMaterial`, `sizeAttenuation: false`) grow with distance.

| Current (`dev`) | Expected |
| --- | --- |
| <img width="776" height="672" alt="On dev, orthographic points shrink and sprites grow with distance" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5093468-f76d-4411-b33b-f19fc79f94c5" /> | <img width="776" height="672" alt="All orthographic points and sprites have the same size" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a49478f-a013-4b9e-a631-20e0424f35b5" /> |

