ISSUE: webpack/webpack#22877: CSS minifier removes the space before `url()` when the URL is an SVG `data:` URL (`transparent url(…)` → `transparenturl(…)`)

### Have you used AI?

Yes

### Which part of webpack is affected?

css

### Bug Description

When the built-in CSS minifier (since 5.110.0) minifies a declaration with a `url()` that holds an **SVG `data:` URL**, it removes the whitespace between `url(` and the component value before it:

```css
/* input */
.b{background:red url("data:image/svg+xml,x")}
/* output */
.b{background:redurl(data:image/svg+xml,x)}
```

`redurl(` tokenizes as a function named `redurl`, so the value no longer parses and browsers drop the whole declaration (checked in Chrome: `new CSSStyleSheet().replaceSync(…)` leaves `cssRules[0].style.cssText` empty). This contradicts the 5.110.0 release note, which says "Minification never changes whether a declaration parses".

We ran into it with Bootstrap's `.btn-close`: `background: transparent url("data:image/svg+xml,…") center/1em auto no-repeat` becomes `background:transparenturl(…)center/1em auto no-repeat`, so the close button's icon disappears.

What triggers it, from varying the input on 5.112.2:

| input | output |
| --- | --- |
| `red url("data:image/svg+xml,x")` | `redurl(data:image/svg+xml,x)` ❌ |
| `no-repeat url("data:image/svg+xml,x")` | `no-repeaturl(data:image/svg+xml,x)` ❌ |
| `red url("data:image/svg+xml;base64,AAAA")` | `redurl(data:image/svg+xml;base64,AAAA)` ❌ |
| `red url("a.svg")` | `red url(a.svg)` ✅ |
| `red url("data:image/png;base64,AAAA")` | `red url(data:image/png;base64,AAAA)` ✅ |
| `red url("data:image/svg,x")`, `red url("data:text/plain,x")` | unchanged ✅ |

Only the `image/svg+xml` media type triggers it. In the same declaration the minifier also percent-decodes the SVG (`%3csvg` → `<svg`), so the SVG `data:` URL goes through a separate rendering path (`builtinEmbeddedRenderer` / the deferred embedded sources in `css/syntax-printer.js`). We haven't traced the code further, so treat that as a pointer, not a diagnosis.

### Link to Minimal Reproduction and steps to reproduce

Four files (inline below):

`package.json`
```json
{
  "private": true,
  "scripts": { "build": "webpack" },
  "devDependencies": {
    "css-loader": "7.1.5",
    "mini-css-extract-plugin": "2.10.2",
    "webpack": "5.112.2",
    "webpack-cli": "7.2.3"
  }
}
```

`webpack.config.js`
```js
const MiniCssExtractPlugin = require('mini-css-extract-plugin');

module.exports = {
  mode: 'production',
  entry: './input.style',
  plugins: [new MiniCssExtractPlugin()],
  module: {
    rules: [{ test: /\.style$/, use: [MiniCssExtractPlugin.loader, { loader: 'css-loader', options: { url: false } }] }],
  },
};
```

`input.style`
```css
.a{background:transparent url("data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'/%3e") center/1em auto no-repeat}
.b{background:red url("data:image/svg+xml,x")}
.c{background:no-repeat url("data:image/svg+xml,x")}
.d{background:red url("a.svg")}
```

Steps:
1. `npm install`
2. `npm run build`
3. Look at `dist/main.css`

Note on the file extension: in our tests the asset is minified only when the source module is **not** a `.css` file. With `test: /\.css$/` and `input.css`, the same input comes out unminified (so the bug does not show), even with `type: 'javascript/auto'`. In our real project the sources are `.scss` (sass-loader), which is how we hit it. If that difference is intentional, ignore this note; otherwise it may deserve its own issue.

### Expected Behavior

Whitespace kept between `url(` and the value before it, as it is for a non-SVG URL:

```css
.b{background:red url(data:image/svg+xml,x)}
.c{background:no-repeat url(data:image/svg+xml,x)}
```

and for `.a` any valid minification, e.g. `background:transparent url("data:…") center/1em auto no-repeat` (with a plain `url("a.png")` the minifier correctly drops the initial `transparent` instead).

### Actual Behavior

```css
.a{background:transparenturl("data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'/>")center/1em auto no-repeat}.b{background:redurl(data:image/svg+xml,x)}.c{background:no-repeaturl(data:image/svg+xml,x)}.d{background:red url(a.svg)}
```

`.a`, `.b` and `.c` are invalid declarations. `.d` (a plain `.svg` file URL) is correct.

### Environment

```shell
System:
  OS:      macOS 26.6.2
  CPU:     (18) arm64 Apple M5 Pro
Binaries:
  Node:  25.9.0
  npm:   11.12.1
Packages:
  css-loader:   7.1.5
  webpack:      5.112.2
  webpack-cli:  7.2.3
```

### Is this a regression?

No

### Last Working Version

_No response_

### Additional Context

Not a regression in the usual sense: the bug has been there since the built-in CSS minification arrived in 5.110.0 (#21841). On this repro, 5.108.0 and 5.109.x leave the asset unminified; 5.110.0 through 5.111.x produce `#0000url(`, `redurl(`, `no-repeaturl(`; 5.112.0 through 5.112.2 produce `transparenturl(`, `redurl(`, `no-repeaturl(`.

Workaround: `optimization.minimize: false` (or configuring a different CSS minimizer).

