ISSUE: JamesNK/Newtonsoft.Json#2921: Unexpected exceptions during deserialization due to missing constructor name

## NullReferenceException
### Sample code

```csharp
using Newtonsoft.Json;

try {
    Console.WriteLine(JsonConvert.DeserializeObject("[new \0("));
} catch (JsonException) {
    Console.WriteLine("invalid JSON");
}
```

### Expected/actual behavior

Should print "invalid JSON". Instead crashes with a `NullReferenceException`.

### Analysis

The crash happens on the expression [`_parent!.Parent`](https://github.com/JamesNK/Newtonsoft.Json/blob/01e1759cac40d8154e47ed0e11c12a9d42d2d0ff/Src/Newtonsoft.Json/Linq/JTokenWriter.cs#L135), so the _damnit_ operator here is inaccurate.

The sequence of events is:
- `JTokenWriter.WriteStartConstructor` invokes [`AddParent(new JConstructor(name))`](https://github.com/JamesNK/Newtonsoft.Json/blob/01e1759cac40d8154e47ed0e11c12a9d42d2d0ff/Src/Newtonsoft.Json/Linq/JTokenWriter.cs#L161) with an empty `name`. This throws an `ArgumentException`, so `AddParent` is not invoked, even though `WriteStartConstructor` has successfully been called
- `JsonWriter.Dispose` is invoked, which does `Close → AutoCompleteAll → WriteEnd → WriteEndConstructor → InternalWriteEnd → AutoCompleteClose → JTokenWriter.WriteEnd → JTokenWriter.RemoveParent`, removing a level of parenting that doesn't exist

### Proposed fixes?

Moving the `new JConstructor` call to the start of `WriteStartConstructor` validates the name before `WriteStartConstructor` is invoked. This stops the NRE but still raises an `ArgumentException` instead of a `JsonException`. Probably the validation of the constructor name should happen much earlier, during reading not writing.

Also, should `JsonWriter` be completing its work if there is an exception in-flight?

## ArgumentException

It is also possible to surface the `ArgumentException` itself via:

```csharp
using Newtonsoft.Json;

try {
    Console.WriteLine(JsonConvert.DeserializeObject("{' ':new \0("));
} catch (JsonException) {
    Console.WriteLine("invalid JSON");
}
```

### Expected/actual behavior

Should print "invalid JSON". Instead crashes with a `ArgumentException` ("Constructor name cannot be empty").

### Analysis

Underlying cause is the same as previous but this one avoids the call to `Dispose` so it doesn’t trigger the NRE.

----

**Credit**: Found via [LibFuzzer](https://llvm.org/docs/LibFuzzer.html) & [SharpFuzz](https://github.com/Metalnem/sharpfuzz).

