ISSUE: jestjs/jest#15730: [Bug]: Jest 30 environment teardown error handling regression

## Version
Jest 30.0.4 (also tested with 29.x for comparison)

## Steps to reproduce
1. Clone the repo at https://github.com/noomorph/jest-env-teardown-error
2. Run `npm install` in the root (installs both subprojects)
3. Run `npm --prefix expected-29 test` (Jest 29, expected behavior)
4. Run `npm --prefix actual-30 test` (Jest 30, shows the bug)
5. (Optional) Run `npm --prefix actual-30 run patch` then `npm --prefix actual-30 test` to see the patched/fixed behavior

## Minimal reproduction

Both subprojects use this custom environment:

```js
const NodeEnvironment = require('jest-environment-node').default;

class CustomEnvironment extends NodeEnvironment {
  async teardown() {
    await super.teardown();
    throw new Error('test');
  }
}

module.exports = CustomEnvironment;
```

And this trivial test:

```js
function hello() {
  return 'Hello, world!';
}

test('hello returns Hello, world!', () => {
  expect(hello()).toBe('Hello, world!');
});
```

## Expected behavior

Jest should report the error thrown from the custom environment's `teardown()` method, as in Jest 29:

```
FAIL  ./hello.test.js
  ● Test suite failed to run

    test

      3 | class CustomEnvironment extends NodeEnvironment {
      4 |   async teardown() {
    > 5 |     await super.teardown();
        |           ^
      6 |     throw new Error('test');
      7 |   }
      8 | }

      at CustomEnvironment.teardown (custom-environment.js:5:11)

Test Suites: 1 failed, 1 total
Tests:       0 total
Snapshots:   0 total
Time:        0.242 s
Ran all test suites.
```

## Actual behavior (Jest 30)

Instead, Jest 30 fails with an internal error:

```
FAIL  ./hello.test.js
  ● Test suite failed to run

    TypeError: The "object" argument must be of type object. Received null

      at tearDownEnv (node_modules/jest-runner/build/index.js:205:34)

Test Suites: 1 failed, 1 total
Tests:       0 total
Snapshots:   0 total
Time:        0.189 s
Ran all test suites.
```

## Why this happens

In Jest 30, the runner calls `tearDownEnv()` both after the test and again in a `finally` block. If the first call to `environment.teardown()` throws, `isTornDown` is never set to `true`, so the second call tries to teardown again, but the environment is already partially destroyed, leading to a confusing internal error:

```js
try {
  ...
  await tearDownEnv(); // <-- first call
  return ...;
} finally {
  await tearDownEnv(); // <-- second call
}
```

## Patch

A minimal patch to `jest-runner` fixes this by ensuring `isTornDown = true` is set in a `finally` block, even if `teardown()` throws, preventing double teardown and restoring the expected error reporting:

```diff
-      await environment.teardown();
-      isTornDown = true;
+      try {
+        await environment.teardown();
+      } finally {
+        isTornDown = true;
+      }
```

See [`actual-30/patches/jest-runner+30.0.4.patch`](actual-30/patches/jest-runner+30.0.4.patch) for details.

