ISSUE: nlohmann/json#5994: json_view: dump() requires StringType::capacity(), which the documented StringType contract (the tests' alt_string) does not provide

### Description

`basic_json_view::dump()` (json_view, merged 2026-10-21) does not compile with a `StringType` that satisfies the documented StringType requirements but has no `capacity()` member. The library's own reference for the minimal `StringType` is the `alt_string` class in `tests/src/unit-alt-string.cpp`: `basic_json<std::map, std::vector, alt_string>` compiles and passes its unit test, but `basic_json_document<...>::parse(...)` followed by `root().dump()` fails with

```
include/nlohmann/detail/view/serializer.hpp:120:83: error: no member named 'capacity' in 'alt_string'
```

`capacity()` is the only missing piece: with a one-line `capacity()` added to `alt_string`, parse, dump (plain, indented, ensure_ascii), materialize, `get<alt_json>`, `find`/`at`/`operator[]`/`contains`/`count` with `alt_string` keys, `items()`, `shrink_to_fit()`, `memory_usage()`, and the editable document's `set`/`push_back`/`save()`/`load()` all compile and run correctly.

The DOM never calls `capacity()` on `string_t`; the StringType section of `docs/mkdocs/docs/features/types/template_parameters.md` does not list it (it lists `reserve(n)` only for "JSON Pointer, flatten, diff", so the view's `reserve()` call is a second requirement the docs do not tie to dump; `alt_string` happens to have it). Nothing under `docs/mkdocs/docs/api/basic_json_view`, `basic_json_document` or `features/json_view.md` mentions StringType requirements, and no json_view test instantiates `alt_string`, which is why CI did not catch it.

### Reproduction steps

```sh
clang++ -std=c++17 -I include -I tests/src view_alt.cpp   # alt_string copied from tests/src/unit-alt-string.cpp
```

### Expected vs. actual results

Expected: json_view compiles with every `StringType` that `basic_json` accepts (or the extra requirement is documented in `template_parameters.md` and checked by a test).

Actual: compile error in `detail/view/serializer.hpp:120`.

### Minimal code example

```cpp
#include <map>
#include <vector>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp>
#include <nlohmann/json_view.hpp>
#include "alt_string.hpp"   // the class from tests/src/unit-alt-string.cpp
using alt_json = nlohmann::basic_json<std::map, std::vector, alt_string>;
int main()
{
    auto d = nlohmann::basic_json_document<alt_json, nlohmann::view_mode::read_only>::parse("{\"a\":[1,\"x\"]}");
    alt_json m = d.root().materialize();   // fine
    (void)d.root().dump();                 // error: no member named 'capacity' in 'alt_string'
}
```

### Error messages

```
include/nlohmann/detail/view/serializer.hpp:120:83: error: no member named 'capacity' in 'alt_string'
    const std::size_t size = (std::max)((std::min)(m_out.size() + step, m_out.capacity()), used + n + 256);
```
instantiated from `output_buffer<alt_string>::grow` ← `reserve` ← `dump_text` ← `dump_ascii` ← `basic_json_view::dump` (`json_view.hpp:665`).

### Compiler and operating system

Apple clang 17 (libc++) and gcc 16 (libstdc++); the error is compiler-independent.

### Library version

develop at ddc34f546a (json_view only; 3.12.0 has no json_view).

### Validation

- [x] The bug also occurs if the latest version from the [`develop`](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/tree/develop) branch is used.
- [x] I can successfully [compile and run the unit tests](https://github.com/nlohmann/json#execute-unit-tests).

### Root cause

[`include/nlohmann/detail/view/serializer.hpp:119-123`](https://github.com/nlohmann/json/blob/ddc34f546a/include/nlohmann/detail/view/serializer.hpp#L119-L123): `output_buffer::grow()` compares `m_out.size() + step` with `m_out.capacity()` to decide how much to `reserve()`.

### Suggested fix

Track the reserved size in `output_buffer` itself (`m_reserved`, set after each `reserve()`; the string may reserve more, so this is a lower bound that costs at most one extra `reserve()`), and use it instead of `m_out.capacity()`. Then add an `alt_string` instantiation of json_view (parse, dump, materialize, editable set/push_back, save/load) to the tests, so the view keeps to the same StringType contract as the DOM. If `capacity()` is meant to be required instead, add it to the StringType requirements in `template_parameters.md` and to the tests' `alt_string`.

---
*Found during a bug hunt on develop; written by Claude Code on behalf of @nlohmann.*

